From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: b1air <dimazzzzz342@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:09:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Add workspace_swipe: workspaces that follow the fingers

A horizontal touchpad swipe with the configured number of fingers moves
the active workspace with the fingers and brings its neighbour on the
same output in beside it, as GNOME and Hyprland do. Letting go switches
to the neighbour when the swipe went a fifth of the way across or was
flicked, and slides both back otherwise. Past the last workspace the
screen gives a little and no more; there is no wrapping round.

The axis is decided over the first 12 units of travel. A vertical swipe
with the same fingers is handed back to the usual gesture handling with
the movement so far, so bindgesture swipe:N:up/down keep working.

The switch's own slide (workspace_animation slide) carries both
workspaces on from where the fingers left them. With fading or no
animation, they are put back before switching.

workspace_swipe off|<fingers> [invert], default off. Also
debug_workspace_swipe begin|update|end|cancel, which drives the same
code from IPC for testing without a touchpad.
